  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Art-music movement launched by the Society for Jewish Folk Music, founded in St Petersburg in 1908, whose composers, among them Joel Engel, Joseph Achron, Mikhail Gnesin, Lazare Saminsky and Moshe Milner, arranged and transformed Ashkenazi folk song, cantorial modes and Hasidic melody into art songs, piano pieces and chamber works in a late-Romantic idiom. The touring Zimro chamber ensemble spread the repertoire abroad, and many of the composers emigrated to Palestine, Western Europe and the United States in the 1920s.",
